            0.83,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Hidato, a grid of cells is given. It is usually square-shaped, like Sudoku or Kakuro, but it can also include hexagons or any shape that forms a tessellation. It can have inner holes (like a disc), but it is made of only one piece."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.156,
            0.829,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Usually, in every Hidato puzzle the lowest and the highest numbers are given on the grid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.194,
            0.83,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Your task is to fill the grid such that there is a continuous path of consecutive numbers from the lowest to the highest number. The next number must be in any one of the adjacent cells, including diagonally adjacent cells."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.271,
            0.83,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The grid comes pre-filled with some numbers (with values between the smallest and the highest) to ensure that these puzzles have a single solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.328,
            0.592,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try solving the following Hidato puzzles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
